 47   C  TITL$NUCLEAR DATA SHEETS FOR A= 47                                     
 47   c  AUTH$S. Ota and E.A. McCutchan                                         
 47   c  INST$National Nuclear Data Center                                      
 47  #c       Brookhaven National Laboratory                                    
 47  #c       Upton, New York 11973-5000, USA                                   
 47   c  ABST$Spectroscopic data for all nuclei with mass number A=47 have been 
 47  2c  evaluated and the corresponding level schemes from radioactive decay   
 47  3c  and reaction studies are presented.  Highlights from this evaluation   
 47  4c  include first observation of gamma-ray transitions in {+47}Ar, a new   
 47  5c  high precision measurement of {+47}K |b decay, and first observation   
 47  6c  of excited levels and gamma-ray transitions in {+47}Mn.                
 47   c  COMM$This work                                                         
 47  1c  supersedes the earlier full evaluation of A=47 by T.W. Burrows         
 47  2c  (2007Bu08), and benefited tremendously from all previous evaluations   
 47  3c  of A= 47.                                                              
 47   c  CIT$NDS 203, 1 (2025)                                                  
 47   c  CUT$All data received by April 1, 2025 have been evaluated.  Main      
 47  2c  bibliographic source was the NSR database (2014Pr09) at Brookhaven     
 47  3c  Laboratory webpage: www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr                               
 47   c  ACKN$The authors thank the reviewer for useful comments on the         
 47  2c  manuscript and are grateful to B. Singh, J. Chen and collaborators for 
 47  3c  A= 47 XUNDL compilations.                                              
 47   c  FUND$Research sponsored by Office of Nuclear Physics, Office of        
 47  xc  Science, US Department of Energy, under contract DE-AC02-98CH10946.    

