 47CL c  2021Li58; E=247 MeV/nucleon {+50}Ar beam was produced from             
 47CL2c  fragmentation of 345 MeV/nucleon {+70}Zn beam on {+9}Be target at      
 47CL3c  RIKEN. Secondary target was 151 mm liquid hydrogen with MINOS setup    
 47CL4c  (beam E=184 MeV/nucleon at exit). Scattered ions analyzed with the     
 47CL5c  SAMURAI spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g, recoil-|g using the DALI2+    
 47CL6c  array consisting of 226 NaI(Tl) detectors and momentum distributions   
 47CL7c  with the SAMURAI array. The experiment measured the                    
 47CL8c  {+48}Cl(p,pn){+47}Cl reaction as well.                                 
 47CL cL E$From E|g data                                                        
 47CL cL $Level scheme is very tentative. 2021Li58 propose another level        
 47CL2cL scheme where the 578 and 632 keV transitions depopulate a single       
 47CL3cL level at 632 keV, with the 632|g going to the ground state and the     
 47CL4cL 578|g going to an unobserved level at 56 keV. The 148 keV transition   
 47CL5cL only observed in {+50}Ar(p,2p2n) may not be a ground state             
 47CL6cL transition, but a transition between two low-lying states.             
