 47AR c  2004We09: produced by a pulsed beam of 1.4 GeV protons from the PSB    
 47AR2c  accelerator impinging on a standard ISOLDE uranium carbide graphite    
 47AR3c  target, heated to about 1900|' C. The reaction products diffused from  
 47AR4c  the heated target and effused {Ivia} a low-temperature, water-cooled   
 47AR5c  transfer line to a standard FEBIAD MK-7 plasma ion source, where the   
 47AR6c  ionization by plasma discharge took place. A tungsten converter was    
 47AR7c  placed parallel to the target, allowing one to switch to the neutron   
 47AR8c  irradiation of the target by changing the focus of the proton beam     
 47AR9c  from the target to the converter. Measured E|g, E|b, I|g, I|b, |g|g-   
 47ARac  and |b|g-coin, and T{-1/2} using two Ge detectors and four 1.5-mm      
 47ARbc  thick plastic detectors (for detecting |b{+-}'s).                      
