 47K  c  2013Pa11,2014Pa45,2014Kr04: E(p)=1.4 GeV incident on UC{-x} target at  
 47K 2c  ISOLDE-CERN facility. Fragments diffused out of target and surface     
 47K 3c  ionized, then accelerated to 40 kV, followed by mass separation and    
 47K 4c  bunched by gas-filled Paul Trap (ISCOOL). Hyperfine structure was      
 47K 5c  studied by collinear laser spectroscopy.                               
 47K  c  2021Ko08, 2019Ko19: 1.4 GeV proton beam incident on a UC{-x} target    
 47K 2c  followed by surface ionization and mass separation using a             
 47K 3c  high-resolution separator (HRS). Ions then cooled and bunched in a     
 47K 4c  linear Paul trap (ISCOOL). Laser spectroscopy performed with the       
 47K 5c  Collinear Resonance Ionization Spectroscopy (CRIS) setup at the        
 47K 6c  ISOLDE facility at CERN. Measured energy differences between atomic    
 47K 7c  hyperfine transitions relative to {+39}K; deduced isotope shift and    
 47K 8c  charge radius.                                                         
