 47K  c  2018Br04: Resonant elastic proton scattering on {+46}Ar. An {+46}Ar    
 47K 2c  beam was produced by a 140 MeV/u {+48}Ca beam and reaccelerated to     
 47K 3c  4.6 MeV/u at ReA3, NSCL. Fragments were selected using the A1900       
 47K 4c  fragment separator and identified using a thin ion chamber. Selected   
 47K 5c  beam particles were transported into the active volume of the          
 47K 6c  Active-Target Time Projection Chamber (AT-TPC), filled with isobutane  
 47K 7c  (C{-4}H{-10}) and placed in a uniform magnetic field generated by a    
 47K 8c  solenoidal magnet. Recoiling protons were detected in the sensor       
 47K 9c  plane on the end of AT-TPC, consisting of a mosaic of 10240            
 47K ac  equilateral triangles for x and y position information. Measured       
 47K bc  proton tracks, |s(E{-p}). Deduced resonance energies, widths, J, |p,   
 47K cc  spectroscopic factors from R-Matrix analysis; deduced isobaric         
 47K dc  analogue states in {+47}Ar.                                            
