 47K  c  2001Kr01: (e,e'p) reaction. Measured momentum distributions with       
 47K 2c  the coincidence setup                                                  
 47K 3c  at NIKHEF. 95.2% enriched {+48}Ca foils. Reduced cross sections        
 47K 4c  obtained under parallel kinematic conditions in the range between -60  
 47K 5c  and 260 MeV/C; outgoing proton kinetic energy of 100 MeV. Coulomb      
 47K 6c  Distorted Wave Impulse Approximation (CDWIA) calculations.             
 47K  c  Compared spectroscopic factors to those of 1985Ba14 from (d,{+3}He).   
 47K 2c  Using original analysis of 1985Ba14, S(d,{+3}He)/S(e,e'p) was |?1.5.   
 47K 3c  After reanalysis of the data from 1985Ba14, S(d,{+3}He)/S(e,e'p) was   
 47K 4c  |?1.0 except for two points at 3.42 and 6.87 MeV. 2001Kr01 suggest     
 47K 5c  that the deviation and the relatively small rms radius (3.39 fm {I9})  
 47K 6c  for transition leading to the 3.42 MeV state might indicate some       
 47K 7c  unresolved 1f{-7/2} strength at 3.4 MeV and that the deviation for     
 47K 8c  the very weak transition at 6.87 MeV may be due to the uncertainty in  
 47K 9c  the rms radius (3.41 fm {I14}) that was not well determined in the     
 47K ac  (e,e'p) experiment.                                                    
