 47CA    9BE(48CA,47CAG)               2009Ma16,2017CR03         25NDS    202507
 47CA  H TYP=FUL$AUT=S. Ota and E.A. McCutchan$CIT=NDS 203, 1 (2025)$           
 47CA2 H CUT=1-Apr-2025$                                                        
 47CA c  2009Ma16: A 450 MeV/nucleon                                            
 47CA2c  {+48}Ca beam impinged on a {+9}Be                                      
 47CA3c  secondary reaction target of 1720                                      
 47CA4c  mg/cm{+2} thickness.                                                   
 47CA5c  The {+47}Ca reaction                                                   
 47CA6c  products were identified event-by-event                                
 47CA7c  in the second dipole stage of                                          
 47CA8c  the FRS and transported to the final FRS focus.                        
 47CA9c  Six time-projection chambers,                                          
 47CAac  two before and two after                                               
 47CAbc  the secondary target at S2 and two at S4, provided position and        
 47CAcc  incident as well as emergent angles of primary fragments and reaction  
 47CAdc  residues, respectively, allowing to reconstruct the flight path        
 47CAec  through the experimental setup. This enabled a precise measurement of  
 47CAfc  the longitudinal momentum distributions of the heavy residues coming   
 47CAgc  from the knockout reaction with a relative momentum resolution of      
 47CAhc  2|*10{+-3} (FWHM). Prompt gamma-rays emitted by the reaction products  
 47CAic  were detected with the eight triple-cluster detectors of the Miniball  
 47CAjc  gamma-ray spectrometer.                                                
 47CAkc  Using the 6-fold segmentation                                          
 47CAlc  of the Miniball HPGe crystals                                          
 47CAmc  for the Doppler correction of the gamma-rays, a resolution of |? 40    
 47CAnc  keV (FWHM) at a c.m. gamma-ray energy of about 580 keV was achieved.   
 47CAoc  Measured: E|g, I|g, (fragment)|g coin, momentum distribution.          
 47CA c  2017Cr03: {+48}Ca beam produced in the fragmentation of 140            
 47CA2c  MeV/nucleon {+82}Se primary beam on a 423 mg/cm{+2} thick {+9}Be       
 47CA3c  target, followed by separation of reaction products using the A1900    
 47CA4c  fragment separator at NSCL-MSU facility. The {+48}Ca beam was          
 47CA5c  incident on a 370 mg/cm{+2} thick {+9}Be reaction target located at    
 47CA6c  the target position of the S800 magnetic spectrograph, by which        
 47CA7c  knockout products were analyzed event by event using time of flight    
 47CA8c  (tof) and energy loss (|DE) technique. The prompt |g rays were         
 47CA9c  detected using seven GRETINA modules surrounding the target position   
 47CAac  of the S800 spectrograph. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,                
 47CAbc  ({+47}Ca)|g-coin, and parallel momentum distributions. Deduced         
 47CAcc  levels, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors, and |g-ray yields by       
 47CAdc  fitting the data by GEANT4 simulation of the GRETINA response,         
 47CAec  including |g(|q) distributions of the emitted |g rays.                 
