 47CA c  Two experiments performed at LNL of INFN using PRISMA-CLARA system     
 47CA c  Reactions used: 1. {+64}Ni({+48}Ca,{+47}Ca|g) E=282 MeV, target=0.98   
 47CA2c  mg/cm{+2}. Projectile-like products selected using PRISMA magnetic     
 47CA3c  spectrometer. Measured |g(|q) and |g(lin pol) using CLARA array of 23  
 47CA4c  Compton-suppressed HPGe clover detectors. 2.                           
 47CA5c  {+208}Pb({+48}Ca,{+47}Ca|g) E=310 MeV, target=1.0 mg/cm{+2}            
 47CA6c  evaporated on a 1.0 mg/cm{+2} Ta layer. A 4 mg/cm{+2} Mg foil was      
 47CA7c  used after the target as an energy degrader. Projectile-like products  
 47CA8c  selected using PRISMA magnetic spectrometer. Half-lives of excited     
 47CA9c  states were measured using differential Recoil Distance Doppler Shift  
 47CAac  method by varying the target-to-degrader distance. Comparisons with    
 47CAbc  full {Ifp} shell-model calculations                                    
