 47SC    47CA B- DECAY                 2022AB01,1969WO02,1966FR1425NDS    202507
 47SC  H TYP=FUL$AUT=S. Ota and E.A. McCutchan$CIT=NDS 203, 1 (2025)$           
 47SC2 H CUT=1-Apr-2025$                                                        
 47SC c  1963Fu09: Measured |g|g(|q) lin pol using NaI detectors. Deduced       
 47SC2c  mixing ratio of 489-keV transition.                                    
 47SC c  1966Fr14: {+47}Ca source from neutron irradiation of Ca(NO{-3}){-2}    
 47SC2c  enriched to 20% in {+46}Ca. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(t) using Ge(Li)      
 47SC3c  detector.                                                              
 47SC c  1969Wo02: {+47}Ca source in the form of CaCl{-2}. Measured E|g, I|g    
 47SC2c  using Ge(Li) detector, |g|g coincidences with NaI(Tl) crystal.         
 47SC c  1987Ju04: Measured E|b and |b|g-coincidences using |b spectrometer     
 47SC2c  and NaI(Tl) detector.                                                  
 47SC c  2022Ab01: {+47}Ca source obtained from isotope harvesting at the       
 47SC2c  NSCL, MSU. Production was through {+48}Ca beam with E=140 MeV/nucleon  
 47SC3c  incident on a flowing-water target, followed by chemical separation.   
 47SC4c  Liquid scintillation counting to determine T{-1/2} of {+47}Ca and      
 47SC5c  {+47}Sc. Measured E|g, I|g using HPGe detector.                        
 47SC c  Others: 2021Ay02, 1968Fi04, 1967Be20, 1967Hs03, 1965Ma06               
 47SC cB IB$From intensity balance at each level                                
 47SC cG $1969Wo02 did not observe (I|g<2.|*10{+-5}) the 1766 and 1836 gammas   
 47SC2cG suggested by 1968Fi04                                                  
 47SC cG E$From 1969Wo02, except as noted                                       
 47SC cG M,MR$From the Adopted Gammas. Support provided by this dataset given   
 47SC2cG in the comments.                                                       
 47SC cG E(E)$From 1966Fr14                                                     
