 47V     28SI(28SI,2APG) E=110,115 MEV 2001BR32,2002TO05         25NDS    202507
 47V   H TYP=FUL$AUT=S. Ota and E.A. McCutchan$CIT=NDS 203, 1 (2025)$           
 47V 2 H CUT=1-Apr-2025$                                                        
 47V  c  2001Br32: E({+28}Si)=115 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, and |g|g              
 47V 2c  using GASP spectrometer comprised of 40 Compton-suppressed large       
 47V 3c  volume HPGe detectors and a BGO multiplicity filter with 80 elements.  
 47V 4c  Deduced T{-1/2} of excited states with Doppler shift attenuation method
 47V 5c  (DSAM) using both standard analysis and                                
 47V 6c  narrow gate on transitions below (NGTB) procedure.                     
 47V  c  2002To05: E({+28}Si)=110 MeV. Measured lifetimes by DSAM using EUROBALL
 47V 2c  III array using only cluster and clover Ge detectors. Charge particles 
 47V 3c  detected with ISIS silicon ball (40 |DE/E telescopes) and neutrons with
 47V 4c  the Neutron Wall (50 large volume liquid scintillator detectors).      
 47V 5c  Level scheme proposed by 1998Be69 in {+24}Mg({+28}Si,|ap|g) assumed.   
 47V  c  The level scheme from 2001Br32 agrees with that proposed by            
 47V 2c  1998Ca26 in {+28}Si({+28}Si,2|ap|g) E=125 MeV, with the exception of   
 47V 3c  the 1904|g-1362 sequence. The positive parity band                     
 47V 4c  proposed by 1998Ca26 has been extended to 35/2+.                       
 47V  cG E,RI$From 2001Br32. Percent photon branching ratio from each           
 47V 2cG level are provided since these are reported with uncertainties.        
 47V 2cG Relative intensities are also included in comments. Uncertainties on   
 47V 3cG E|g estimated based on a comment by 2001Br32 that uncertainties are    
 47V 4cG 0.4 keV rising to 1 keV above 2 MeV.                                   
 47V  cG E(A)$Could not be uniquely placed and appeared to enter into the       
 47V 2cG level scheme at the 23/2- state (2001Br32)                             
 47V  cG E(B)$From Figure 1 of 2001Br32, not given in Table 1                   
 47V  cG E(E),RI(F)$Established indirectly by estimating I|g of the 1320 and    
 47V 2cG 1264 |g's in coincidence with the 1518|g                               
 47V  cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g's, by evaluators.                      
 47V  cL J$As given in 2001Br32. As specific arguments were not given by        
 47V 2cL 2001Br32, the J|p assignments appear to be heavily based               
 47V 2cL on previous work.                                                      
