 47V     46TI(P,P),(P,P'):RES                                    25NDS    202507
 47V   H TYP=FUL$AUT=S. Ota and E.A. McCutchan$CIT=NDS 203, 1 (2025)$           
 47V 2 H CUT=1-Apr-2025$                                                        
 47V  c  1961Du03: E(p)=800-1400 keV. Measured excitation functions using       
 47V 2c  magnetic analyzer and NaI detector.                                    
 47V 3c  Observed 30 resonances with an average level spacing of |?13 keV and   
 47V 4c  notes that the natural half-widths of all resonances observed was less 
 47V 5c  than 0.5 keV.                                                          
 47V  c  1969Ky01: E=2.5-2.9 MeV; overall energy resolution|?1700 eV.           
 47V 2c  Measured |g(|q)(889|g) and |g-ray excitation function for the          
 47V 3c  first-excited, 2+, state; NaI. Observed 45 resonances; deduced J|p     
 47V 4c  and resonance parameters.                                              
 47V  c  1971Ka23: E=1350-2280 keV. Measured excitation functions; NaI.         
 47V 2c  Observed 126 resonances in the excitation energy range of 6.5 to 7.4   
 47V 3c  MeV with an average level spacing of |?6 keV. Compared to resonances   
 47V 4c  in {+48}Ti(p,|g). Identified eight prominent resonances as isobaric    
 47V 5c  analogs of states in {+47}Ti.                                          
 47V  c  1973Pr02: E=1.5-3.1 MeV; overall resolution|?300 eV. Measured          
 47V 2c  |s(|q) at four angles. Observed 144 resonances; deduced J|p,           
 47V 3c  resonance parameters, and exit-channel L.                              
 47V  c  1979Ch20: E=2.25-3.10 MeV; overall resolution=350 eV. Measured         
 47V 2c  |s(|q), |g(|q); surface barrier, NaI. Studied (p,p'|g) to the          
 47V 3c  first-excited, 2+, state for 47 L=1 and five L=3 resonances between    
 47V 4c  2.25 and 3.10 MeV. Deduced J|p and resonance parameters.               
 47V  c  See 1977Ha45 for a compilation and comparison of the resonances        
 47V 2c  observed by 1973Pr02, 1971Ka23, 1969Ky01, and 1961Du03. See also       
 47V 3c  {+46}Ti(p,|g) E=0.72-4 MeV and E=0.4-1.8 MeV                           
