 47CR c  1998Be69,1999Be23: {+24}Mg({+28}Si,|an|g), E=87 MeV. Measured E|g,     
 47CR2c  |g|g, particle-|g|g coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO) using pex array of four        
 47CR3c  Euroball cluster detectors. Particles detected using a 31-silicon      
 47CR4c  wafer array for protons and |a's, and a 15-element array of liquid     
 47CR5c  scintillator detectors for neutrons.                                   
 47CR c  2002To05: {+28}Si({+28}Si,2|an|g) E=110 MeV. Measured lifetimes by     
 47CR2c  Doppler-shift attenuation method using Euroball III array using only   
 47CR3c  cluster and clover Ge detectors. Charge particles detected with ISIS   
 47CR4c  silicon ball (40 |DE/E telescopes) and neutrons with the Neutron Wall  
 47CR5c  (50 large volume liquid scintillator detectors).                       
 47CR c  All data from 1998Be69, except as noted. The level scheme is consistent
 47CR2c  with that of 1994Ca04 in {+10}B({+40}Ca,p2n|g) up through the 5902     
 47CR3c  keV, 23/2- state. The present work showed no evidence for the 1823|g   
 47CR4c  assigned as 27/2- to 23/2- by 1994Ca04.                                
